<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/glossary#lukonkesh">Glossary</a> · Term · title</p><h1 class="enc-title">Lukonkesh</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Lukokesha</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Lukonkesh (Lukokesha) was the title of the queen mother of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lunda-empire">Lunda Empire</a> in central <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/africa">Africa</a>, a female dignitary of high rank at the royal capital, the musumba. Regarded as the symbolic mother of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mwaant-yaav">Mwaant Yaav</a>, she held her own court and lands and took part in the council of titled office-holders that advised on succession and other affairs of state.</p></div>
